Package: office-convert
Version: 0.1.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>
Depends: pandoc, python3, python3-openpyxl
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/excelano/office-convert
Description: Converters between plain-text sources and Microsoft Office files
 Five command-line converters between the plain-text formats you author and
 version and their Microsoft Office counterparts: md2docx and docx2md
 (Markdown and Word), csv2xlsx and xlsx2csv (CSV and Excel), and md2pptx
 (Markdown to PowerPoint). PowerPoint is export-only because pandoc writes
 .pptx but cannot read it.
 .
 Each command takes an input file and an optional output path, defaulting to
 the input name with the new extension. md2docx and md2pptx accept a pandoc
 reference document as a style template, and csv2xlsx types cells only when
 the conversion is lossless, so leading-zero codes and long digit runs survive
 the trip into Excel as text.
 .
 The converters reimplement nothing: pandoc does the Markdown, Word, and
 PowerPoint work, and openpyxl does the Excel work.
